config: {}
doc: "Experiment 2: sharded model loading (4 drives, all four loaders).\n\nSharded\
  \ 40 GB Llama-3.3-70B Q4_K_M, one shard per drive\n(c1..c4 -> /mnt/dma-{0..3}).\
  \ Each loader path reads all 40 GB\nfrom the 4-drive fleet:\n\n  - mmap        \
  \                (kernel path, mmap-backed)\n  - stream                      (kernel\
  \ path, read()-based)\n  - xnvme io_uring_file         (kernel path, O_DIRECT)\n\
  \  - upcie-cuda                  (userspace P2P, per-file drive\n              \
  \                   routing)\n\nMPS disabled for consistency with exp1.\n\nNote:\
  \ the upcie-cuda step is preceded by an xnvmeperf-4-URI prime\nstep. Without it,\
  \ the 4-drive registry_init inside llama-completion\nintermittently produces a dev\
  \ with lba_nbytes=0 and falls back to\nstream. Priming with xnvmeperf clears the\
  \ state; root cause TBD."
status:
  elapsed: 126.24026417732239
  failed: 0
  passed: 16
  skipped: 0
  started: 1783517728.34088
steps:
- description: 'One-shot: kill any lingering llama-cli / llama-completion / llama-server
    on the target and dump current GPU memory.'
  id: 001_kill_stray_cuda
  name: kill_stray_cuda
  nr: 1
  status:
    elapsed: 2.0929863452911377
    failed: 0
    passed: 1
    skipped: 0
    started: 1783517728.3415666
  uses: kill_stray_cuda
- description: Turn CUDA MPS off and reset compute mode to DEFAULT so subsequent processes
    see the whole VRAM.
  id: 002_disable_mps
  name: disable_mps
  nr: 2
  status:
    elapsed: 2.24040150642395
    failed: 0
    passed: 1
    skipped: 0
    started: 1783517730.4345667
  uses: disable_mps
- description: "\nPrepare a spare NVMe as the DMA target for xNVMe's upcie-cuda backend.\n\
    \nTwo layout modes are supported. Both end with the drive detached\nfrom the kernel\
    \ NVMe driver and bound to uio_pci_generic, and both\nemit an extents JSON that\
    \ the loader consumes via\nLLAMA_XNVME_DMA_EXTENTS.\n\n  layout=raw (default,\
    \ backwards compatible):\n    Copy the .gguf onto the raw device starting at LBA\
    \ 0 via dd.\n    The drive holds a raw byte image of the file; file offset O\n\
    \    trivially maps to LBA (O / lba_nbytes). The extents JSON has\n    a single\
    \ entry, [{file_offset: 0, lba: 0, length: file_size}].\n\n  layout=xfs-fiemap:\n\
    \    Format XFS on the drive, mount, copy the .gguf onto the FS as\n    a normal\
    \ file, run xfs_bmap (FIEMAP equivalent) to capture the\n    file's on-disk extents,\
    \ umount, then detach + bind as above.\n    The extents JSON carries one entry\
    \ per XFS extent with the\n    per-drive LBA computed from the physical block\
    \ offset. This is\n    the realistic \"user put their model on a real FS\" shape.\n\
    \nIn both modes the workflow's earlier setup_dataset step must have\nstaged the\
    \ model onto a *different* drive (the source drive,\nmounted at /mnt/gguf/model.gguf)\
    \ so llama.cpp can open the file for\nGGUF metadata reads during the run; the\
    \ DMA target here is the only\ndrive touched during bulk weight reads.\n"
  id: 003_prepare_dma_c1
  name: prepare_dma_c1
  nr: 3
  status:
    elapsed: 10.593245267868042
    failed: 0
    passed: 1
    skipped: 0
    started: 1783517732.6749852
  uses: setup_dma_target
  with:
    defer_detach: 'true'
    dma_namespace: 1
    dma_pci_addr: 0000:c1:00.0
    fs_dst_name: shard.gguf
    fs_mount_point: /mnt/dma-0
    gguf_extents_path: /root/dma-c1.extents.json
    layout: xfs-fiemap
    source_gguf: /mnt/gguf-src/Llama-3.3-70B-Q4_K_M-00001-of-00004.gguf
