- description: 'Create a symlink directory that presents shards on several mounts
    as one directory.


    llama.cpp discovers sibling shards of a split GGUF by walking the

    ``basename-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf`` pattern in the same directory. When

    each shard lives on its own mount for parallel-drive load, we still

    need one directory that presents all N shards side by side. This

    script creates that directory of symlinks; the kernel resolves each

    symlink to the underlying mount at open time, so reads land on the

    right drive.

    '
  id: 007_setup_shard_symlinks
  name: setup_shard_symlinks
  nr: 7
  status:
    elapsed: 1.5773887634277344
    failed: 0
    passed: 1
    skipped: 0
    started: 1783517774.2699971
  uses: setup_shard_symlinks
  with:
    basename: Llama-3.3-70B-Q4_K_M
    shard_paths: /mnt/dma-0/shard.gguf,/mnt/dma-1/shard.gguf,/mnt/dma-2/shard.gguf,/mnt/dma-3/shard.gguf
    symlink_dir: /mnt/gguf-shards
- description: "\nCold-start measurement for llama.cpp with a configurable loader\
    \ path.\n\nDrops the OS page cache before each iteration, runs llama-completion\n\
    with ``-n 1`` so it stops as soon as one token is produced, and\nrecords the wall-clock\
    \ and max RSS via /usr/bin/time. The interval\nis dominated by the weight-load\
    \ phase, so it is the \"seconds to\nfirst token\" figure of merit.\n\nThe same\
    \ script drives every loader variant so their cijoe outputs\nland side by side\
    \ under the same step template. Pass:\n\n    loader:    mmap | stream | xnvme\
    \ | default\n    direct_io: true | false\n    xnvme_be:  io_uring_file | libaio_file\
    \ | thrpool_file | ...\n\nUses llama-completion rather than llama-cli because\
    \ upstream\nrefactored llama-cli into a chat-only REPL; llama-completion is the\n\
    tty-free one-shot binary.\n"
  id: 008_run_mmap
  name: run_mmap
  nr: 8
  status:
    elapsed: 19.572150945663452
    failed: 0
    passed: 1
    skipped: 0
    started: 1783517775.847398
  uses: run_baseline
  with:
    gguf_path: /mnt/gguf-shards/Llama-3.3-70B-Q4_K_M-00001-of-00004.gguf
    iterations: 1
    llama_bin: /root/llama.cpp/build/bin/llama-completion
    loader: mmap
    n_gpu_layers: 999
    n_tokens: 1
    prompt: hi
